# Coding Standards and Best Practices

## JavaScript/Vue Coding Standards
- Project follows the Vue.js Style Guide
- ESLint is configured with Standard style and Vue plugin
- See [.eslintrc.js](mdc:.eslintrc.js) for specific rules

## ESLint Rules
Key ESLint rules include:
- Vue Essential (Priority A: Error Prevention)
- Standard JS style
- Import/export validation

## Linting
- Run `yarn lint` to check for linting issues
- ESLint is also integrated into the build process

## Git Workflow
- Project uses conventional commits enforced by commitlint
- See [commitlint.config.js](mdc:commitlint.config.js) for configuration
- Husky is used for git hooks

## Code Organization
- Vue components should be modular and reusable
- Use mixins for shared functionality
- Store modules should be namespaced
- Follow Quasar recommended practices for components and layouts
